WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.150
Your calculator says sine of seventy-five
degrees is nought point nine six five

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.120
nine, and the digits just keep going.

3
00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.880
Then the exam paper says:
give the exact value.

4
00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.600
And there's no calculator.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.720
So how could anyone know that
never-ending decimal exactly?

6
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.620
In this mission, you'll start from
exact values you already know,

7
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.820
for thirty, forty-five and sixty degrees.

8
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.450
And seventy-five degrees
is forty-five plus thirty.

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.600
But careful: sine of A plus
B is not sine A plus sine B.

10
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:38.860
Instead, compound angle identities turn
one ratio you don't know into ratios you

11
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.760
do.

12
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.980
Your mission: work out how you could find
sine of seventy-five degrees exactly,

13
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.370
without a calculator.
